# Through the Breach's "Sacrifice that creature at the beginning of the next end step" follows the object it put onto
# the battlefield. On turn five Bot1 casts Displacer Kitten, then Through the Breach (the Kitten's trigger on that cast
# targets nothing) and puts Griselbrand in with haste. A third Black Lotus is a noncreature spell, and the Kitten's
# trigger on it blinks Griselbrand: it returns as a new object (CR 400.7), without the haste, and the delayed
# sacrifice no longer refers to it. It survives the end step and is still there on Bot2's turn.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Island
Mountain
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Displacer Kitten
Through the Breach
Griselbrand
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

